= P-192 ray-character square grid
#text(fill: rgb("64748b"))[Exact coverage and point-work gate · 2026-11-23 PST · [pcc:unverified]]

== Question and construction
This report tests whether a point-dependent sign in the P-192 prime-order subgroup can be evaluated below the reference expected rho work. It screens the square-class grid generated by public integers 2 and 5; the full scope and reproduction instructions are in #link("REPORT.md")[REPORT.md]. The subgroup order is $r=6277101735386680763835789423176059013767194773182842284081$ and the square-label quotient has $N=(r-1)/4=1569275433846670190958947355794014753441798693295710571020$ labels.

Because 2 and 5 are squares modulo $r$, write $2^c=plus.minus 5 mod r$. Here $c$ is a public finite-field logarithm, distinct from the elliptic-curve scalar. Table length $M$ and query length $L$ yield intervals $[c j,c j+M-1] mod N$ for $0 <= j < L$. A collision of marked point multiples certifies the positive character; a negative result is decisive only after the intervals cover all $N$ labels.

